  "title": "Dataset Clinical Epilepsy iEEG to BIDS - RESPect_longterm_iEEG",
  "description": "This dataset contains clinical intracranial EEG (iEEG) recordings from 12 epilepsy surgery patients, part of the RESPect (Registry for Epilepsy Surgery Patients) registry at University Medical Center Utrecht. Six patients were recorded intraoperatively with acute ECoG, and six had long-term monitoring (three with ECoG, three with SEEG). The data are organized in BIDS using session and run conventions that encode the surgical situation or the monitoring day and time. The dataset also includes anatomical MRI and FreeSurfer-derived surface and segmentation files.",
  "methods_description": "Intraoperative ECoG recordings are grouped into BIDS sessions by surgical phase (pre-resection, intermediate, post-resection) and by grid/strip position. Long-term recordings are grouped by monitoring period, with the run label encoding the day and start time. The task label describes the patient's state, such as rest, sleep, or clinical SPES.",
